Yes. Your current pipeline is correct for **ascending** order:

```java
numberList.stream()
        .filter(i -> i % 2 == 0)
        .sorted()
        .forEach(System.out::println);
```

### Descending order

Since `Integer` implements `Comparable`, you can use:

```java
numberList.stream()
        .filter(i -> i % 2 == 0)
        .sorted(Comparator.reverseOrder())
        .forEach(System.out::println);
```

Or:

```java
.sorted(Comparator.comparingInt(Integer::intValue).reversed())
```

But for integers, **`Comparator.reverseOrder()` is the cleanest.**

### Your complete code

```java
numberList.stream()
        .filter(i -> i % 2 == 0)
        .sorted(Comparator.reverseOrder())
        .forEach(System.out::println);
```

Output starts:

```text
98
96
94
92
...
4
2
0
```

